vcraps for OS-9/68000=====================ORIG holds comp.sources.games volume 11, vcraps version 2 (two parts), asposted, with its two patch files.  The files beside it are those sourceswith patches01 and then patches02 applied (both apply cleanly), and thechanges below.What changed, and why:  recipe     -Drandom=rand -Dsrandom=srand: the default libraries have no             random().  -D_maxx=w_cols: Microware's WINDOW calls the width             w_cols.  vcraps.c   `case '\r':' is left out under OSK, because '\n' and '\r' are             both 13 here and the compiler rejects the duplicate case; the             '\n' case already takes Return.             OS-9's terminal driver takes ESC as end of file, so ESC never             reached Getch() and could not abort an entry (measured: a bet             prompt stayed open).  vcraps_tty() clears that one setting             before initscr(), because curses rewrites the saved settings             on every noecho(), and deinit() puts back only that field.  getopt.c   The default libraries have no getopt(); this is the one from             SRC/arithmetic.crapslib.c, crapslib.h and patchlevel.h build as patched, unchanged.vcraps.c calls bcopy(), which the default libraries lack; the build driversupplies it from SRC/COMPAT (os9bcopy.c).Build: cc vcraps.c crapslib.c getopt.c -DOSK -Drandom=rand -Dsrandom=srand          -D_maxx=w_cols -l=curses.l -l=termlib.l